                        "name": "Min Wang",
                        "email": "wangmin@phytium.com.cn",
                        "username": "wangmin239"
                    },
                    "message": "I\u2019ve gone through the code thoroughly and added my review notes. Feel free to reach out if you have any questions about my suggestions."
                },
                {
                    "file": "keymap.cpp",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Min Wang",
                        "email": "wangmin@phytium.com.cn",
                        "username": "wangmin239"
                    },
                    "message": "Try swapping lines 13\u201347 with the snippet below.\n\nstatic constexpr int NUM_MODIFIER_BITS = 8;\nstatic constexpr std::pair<rfbKeySym, uint8_t> keyModMap[NUM_MODIFIER_BITS] = {\n    {XK_Shift_L,    USBHID_KEY_SHIFT_L  },\n    {XK_Shift_R,    USBHID_KEY_SHIFT_R  },\n    {XK_Control_L,  USBHID_KEY_CONTROL_L},\n    {XK_Control_R,  USBHID_KEY_CONTROL_R},\n    {XK_Meta_L,     USBHID_Meta_L       },\n    {XK_Meta_R,     USBHID_Meta_R       },\n    {XK_Alt_L,      USBHID_Alt_L        },\n    {XK_Alt_R,      USBHID_Alt_R        }\n};\n\nuint8_t keyToMod(rfbKeySym key)\n{\n    uint8_t mod = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < NUM_MODIFIER_BITS; ++i) {\n        if (key == keyModMap[i].first) {\n            mod = keyModMap[i].second;\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n    return mod;\n}"
                },
                {
                    "file": "keymap.cpp",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jae Hyun Yoo",
                        "email": "jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com",
                        "username": "jaehyoo"
                    },
                    "message": "The primary purpose of this MR was actually to add unit tests for the key input logic, so this kind of refactoring would normally belong in a separate commit.  However, since I was already touching the source structure, I went ahead and included it as well. As you suggested, I updated the code to use macros for the modifier key bits."
                },
                {
                    "file": "keymap.cpp",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Min Wang",
                        "email": "wangmin@phytium.com.cn",
                        "username": "wangmin239"
                    },
                    "message": "Sorry I misread your original plan. This refactor looks really clean, nice job adopting the modifier key macros as we discussed."
                },
                {
                    "file": "keymap.cpp",
                    "line": 72,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Min Wang",
                        "email": "wangmin@phytium.com.cn",
                        "username": "wangmin239"
                    },
                    "message": "Since this function is overly long, it\u2019s best to split the code from line 74 to line 250 into multiple dedicated functions."
                },
                {
                    "file": "keymap.cpp",
                    "line": 72,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jae Hyun Yoo",
                        "email": "jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com",
                        "username": "jaehyoo"
                    },
                    "message": "Okay, let's refactor this as well.  I split the logic into helper functions based on the key categories to make the code cleaner and easier to follow."
                },
                {
